Hi Aurelie:

ggplot2-0.9.0 is currently the development version of the software,
but as Winston mentioned, it should be sent to CRAN 'real soon now'
and hopefully make it past the security gate. If all goes well, you
should be able to install it tomorrow or the day after from the CRAN
mirrors. If you can't wait that long, then try this, which requires
the devtools and scales packages:

# install.packages('devtools')     #  uncomment if not installed on your system
library('devtools')
dev_mode()    # should reply dev_mode: ON
install_github('ggplot2')
install_github('scales')
library('ggplot2')
library('scales')
<your code here>

dev_mode() basically allows you to install development versions of R
packages not yet released to CRAN and keeps them separate from the
official CRAN versions. When dev_mode is ON, the development version
of packages is used; if OFF, the CRAN versions are used. If dev_mode
is OFF, the install_github() lines will overwrite the old versions,
which you may or may not want.

Dennis

