Hm, it looks like both the faceting and the inherited group aes were an issue... it was faceting on month, but div0A_merged didn't have a month column, and I guess ggplot2 0.8.9 doesn't like it when you facet on a non-existing variable.

Here's a way to add a month column to the data frame, and replicate each row for each month:

# Get all the months used in OTc
monthdf <- data.frame(month = unique(OTc$month))

# Merge with div0A_merged
# (replicate each row in div0A_merged for each month)
div0A_merged_month <- merge(div0A_merged, monthdf)

# Graph with the shapefile

ggplot(div0A_merged_month, aes(long, lat, group=group)) +
  geom_polygon() +
  geom_path(color="white") +
  geom_point(data=OTc, aes(x=longitude, y=latitude, size=TSUM),

             colour="red", alpha=0.2, inherit.aes=FALSE) +

  theme_bw() +
  facet_wrap(~ month, ncol=2)

Or of course you could install 0.9.0, as Dennis described.

-Winston

