I'm plotting some data, where facets have a "location" name. Several location levels have a localized character (š, č or ž) and I've noticed they are not displayed correctly. I've fiddled around with options("encoding" = "UTF-8") but got me nowhere. Has anyone experienced a similar problem and maybe found a way how to circumvent it? I've had a similar problem <http://stackoverflow.com/questions/3434349/sweave-not-printing-localized-characters> with writing to a pdf a while ago.

For instance, this facet should read "Menišija", but instead I get "MeniL..ija" (š was translated to "L..").

Any advice much appreciated.

Cheers,
Roman

