I've coded up a stat_summaryGroup which behaves as I want - is it
appropriate to post it here?  It's based upon stat_summary code.

used like this:

> qplot(data=diamonds,carat,price,label=color,group=color)+geom_text(color="red",stat="summaryGroup",fun.x=mean,fun.y=mean)

-Alex

On Mar 16, 10:16 am, "Alex@775" <alexbbr...@gmail.com> wrote:
> That is pretty awesome, thanks.  I shall probably use this on
> occasion.
>
> > q = ggplot(mtcars, aes(x = wt, y=mpg, group=cyl)) + geom_point() + geom_smooth(se=F, method="lm", formula=y~1)
> > q
>
> It does feel a bit cheaty.
>
> It goes a bit wrong if I want to annotate with text - it turns out
> smooth generates multiple points.
>
> > q = ggplot(mtcars, aes(x = wt, y=mpg, group=cyl)) + geom_point() + stat_smooth(se=F, method="lm", formula=y~1, aes(label=sprintf("%.2f",..y..)), geom=c("text","hline"))
> > q
>
> It also only deals with one dimension - I may want to position x and y
