On 2012-Mar-19, at 14:37 , Heike Hofmann wrote:
>
> you can use qplot for showing multiple time series - the easiest way would be to melt the variables into a single variable and then plot:
>
> X1 <- rnorm(100)
> X2 <- rnorm(mean=3, 100)
> X3 <- rnorm(mean=1, 100)
> frame <- data.frame(X1=X1, X2=X2, X3=X3)
>
>
> library(ggplot2)
> frame$id <- 1:nrow(frame)
> framem <- melt(frame, measure.vars=1:3)
> qplot(id, value, group=variable, geom="line", colour=variable, data=framem)

That's fine if your series have the same units, but that does not seems to be the case in your example data frame. In that situation, consider using facets (facet_grid() or facet_wrap()) with the argument scales="free_y".

