Use
	scale_fill_gradient2 with the low, mid, and high and define the midpoint explicitly
or
	scale_fill_gradientn with a diverging sequence of colours, if you don't want to pick the midpoint explicitly. colours are used in the order in which they are specified. In you example, we don't know where the pal() function comes from. You can use rev(pal(7)) to reverse the vector of colours or use something like c("red","white","blue") as the colours argument

